<i>‪and kept forcing the numbers to fit,</i>

434
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:44,011
<i>‪so of course nothing worked.</i>

435
00:21:44,511 --> 00:21:47,597
<i>‪I counted all five shapes first.</i>

436
00:21:47,681 --> 00:21:50,225
<i>‪The second-most-common shape</i>
<i>‪turned out to be a circle.</i>

437
00:21:50,309 --> 00:21:51,560
<i>‪Then I looked for circles</i>

438
00:21:51,643 --> 00:21:55,105
<i>‪where the difference</i>
<i>‪between the second and fourth numbers</i>

439
00:21:55,188 --> 00:21:57,274
<i>‪was seven.</i>

440
00:21:57,357 --> 00:22:01,528
<i>‪I spotted 15 and 22, so I locked those in.</i>

441
00:22:02,487 --> 00:22:04,031
‪Ten, eight.

442
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:06,158
‪"Three shapes."

443
00:22:09,703 --> 00:22:11,663
<i>‪I chose eight and ten</i>
<i>‪and </i><i>‪thought </i><i>‪it </i><i>‪was </i><i>‪right.</i>

444
00:22:11,747 --> 00:22:13,790
<i>‪So I was about to press the buzzer</i>
<i>‪when I remembered…</i>

445
00:22:13,874 --> 00:22:17,336
‪Wait, the shape
‪on the second-lowest card is…

446
00:22:17,919 --> 00:22:21,506
<i>‪If I had set up a few equations,</i>
<i>‪I could've narrowed it down quickly.</i>

447
00:22:21,590 --> 00:22:22,841
<i>‪But that didn't occur to me,</i>

448
00:22:22,924 --> 00:22:25,969
<i>‪so I ended up plugging in numbers,</i>
<i>‪which took longer than expected.</i>

449
00:22:34,269 --> 00:22:37,147
<i>‪While I was verifying my answer…</i>

450
00:22:39,649 --> 00:22:40,525
<i>‪JAE JAE.</i>

451
00:22:41,735 --> 00:22:43,403
<i>‪JAE JAE pressed her buzzer.</i>

452
00:22:45,072 --> 00:22:46,990
‪A, O, Q, V.

453
00:22:49,993 --> 00:22:51,411
<i>‪Correct.</i>

454
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:53,622
<i>‪You have survived.</i>

455
00:22:53,705 --> 00:22:56,041
<i>‪Please remain at your spot.</i>

456
00:22:56,124 --> 00:22:57,876
<i>‪I thought it'd be a race against time,</i>

457
00:22:57,959 --> 00:23:02,047
‪but the conditions were so precise
‪that I realized accuracy matters.

458
00:23:02,130 --> 00:23:05,258
<i>‪Cards 15 and 22 were locked in.</i>

459
00:23:05,342 --> 00:23:07,469
<i>‪The total sum had to be 55.</i>

460
00:23:07,552 --> 00:23:09,805
<i>‪Since 55 minus 37 gives you 18,</i>

461
00:23:09,888 --> 00:23:12,891
<i>‪I realized the first and third numbers</i>
<i>‪had to add up to 18.</i>

462
00:23:12,974 --> 00:23:14,518
<i>‪With the second-lowest number at 15,</i>

463
00:23:14,601 --> 00:23:17,145
<i>‪the third-lowest had to be larger than 15,</i>
<i>‪which led me to cards 16 and 2.</i>

464
00:23:17,813 --> 00:23:19,231
<i>‪But that didn't satisfy</i>
<i>‪the </i><i>‪third </i><i>‪condition.</i>

465
00:23:19,314 --> 00:23:22,901
<i>‪When I tried cards 1 and 17,</i>
<i>‪it worked, so I hit the buzzer.</i>

466
00:23:22,984 --> 00:23:28,907
‪It felt so freaking amazing
‪when they said it was the correct answer.

467
00:23:29,407 --> 00:23:31,993
<i>‪The answer I was verifying</i>
<i>‪turned out to be right.</i>

468
00:23:32,077 --> 00:23:35,288
‪So I thought, "Darn it.
‪If only I'd been 30 seconds faster."

469
00:23:36,873 --> 00:23:39,960
<i>‪I think I was very nervous</i>
<i>‪in the beginning.</i>

470
00:23:41,002 --> 00:23:45,340
‪JAE JAE hit the buzzer
‪before I even got to the other conditions.

471
00:23:45,423 --> 00:23:48,135
‪I wasn't even close to getting the answer,

472
00:23:48,218 --> 00:23:50,846
‪and it was already over.

473
00:23:51,429 --> 00:23:53,390
<i>‪Round 2 will now begin.</i>

474
00:23:53,974 --> 00:23:55,767
<i>‪Here is the prompt.</i>

475
00:23:56,268 --> 00:23:57,978
‪① THE SUM OF 4 NUMBERS IS 54,
‪② 4 COLORS, ③ 2 SHAPES,

476
00:23:58,061 --> 00:23:59,855
‪④ THE PRODUCT OF THE 1ST
‪AND 4TH CARDS IS 50 OR BELOW,

477
00:23:59,938 --> 00:24:01,940
‪⑤ THE SUM OF THE HIGHEST
‪AND THE LOWEST NUMBERS IS 20 OR ABOVE,

478
00:24:02,023 --> 00:24:04,151
‪⑥ THE COLOR OF THE THIRD-LOWEST CARD
‪IS THE LEAST COMMON COLOR

479
00:24:04,234 --> 00:24:07,863
<i>‪It was a bit more complex than Round 1.</i>

480
00:24:07,946 --> 00:24:11,700
<i>‪The sum of the highest and lowest numbers</i>

481
00:24:11,783 --> 00:24:15,537
<i>‪had to be 20 or above,</i>
<i>‪while the product had to be 50 or below.</i>

482
00:24:15,620 --> 00:24:17,998
<i>‪I figured there couldn't be</i>
<i>‪that many combinations,</i>

483
00:24:18,081 --> 00:24:19,708
<i>‪so I started there.</i>

484
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:26,214
‪SUM: 19

485
00:24:29,551 --> 00:24:30,385
‪Damn it.

486
00:24:30,927 --> 00:24:32,345
‪What was it again? Damn it.

487
00:24:33,221 --> 00:24:34,306
‪What was it?

488
00:24:34,389 --> 00:24:36,933
‪Fifty-four, thirty-one.

489
00:24:37,601 --> 00:24:39,352
<i>‪For some strange reason,</i>

490
00:24:39,436 --> 00:24:42,147
<i>‪it was so much harder to calculate</i>
<i>‪while standing on that platform.</i>

491
00:24:42,230 --> 00:24:43,231
<i>‪It was so weird.</i>

492
00:24:44,191 --> 00:24:45,066
‪Hold on.

493
00:24:53,825 --> 00:24:54,910
‪Three, twelve…

494
00:24:54,993 --> 00:24:57,621
‪SUM: 44

495
00:24:57,704 --> 00:24:59,331
‪Damn it.

496
00:25:02,792 --> 00:25:04,502
‪The W card is yellow,
‪so that won't work.

497
00:25:04,586 --> 00:25:05,962
‪② 4 COLORS

498
00:25:08,590 --> 00:25:11,760
<i>‪I just didn't wanna come in last.</i>

499
00:25:11,843 --> 00:25:13,345
<i>‪It was really nerve-racking.</i>

500
00:25:15,388 --> 00:25:18,058
‪④ THE PRODUCT OF THE 1ST
‪AND 4TH CARDS IS 50 OR BELOW

501
00:25:20,685 --> 00:25:21,895
‪Hang on.

502
00:25:31,780 --> 00:25:34,908
<i>‪Ha Seok-jin, please state your answer.</i>

503
00:25:36,201 --> 00:25:37,160
‪A, N,

504
00:25:38,578 --> 00:25:39,704
‪P, W.

505
00:25:43,208 --> 00:25:44,334
<i>‪Correct.</i>

506
00:25:44,417 --> 00:25:46,962
<i>‪You have survived.</i>

507
00:25:47,045 --> 00:25:49,130
<i>‪Please remain at your spot.</i>

508
00:25:49,923 --> 00:25:52,467
<i>‪I verified it over and over.</i>

509
00:25:52,550 --> 00:25:55,178
<i>‪Right up until I hit the buzzer,</i>

510
00:25:55,262 --> 00:25:57,347
<i>‪my mouth was completely dry.</i>

511
00:25:59,307 --> 00:26:00,976
‪Why is this making me so nervous?

512
00:26:01,059 --> 00:26:02,894
‪I bet my cortisol was through the roof.

513
00:26:06,231 --> 00:26:08,400
<i>‪Round 3 will now begin.</i>

514
00:26:08,900 --> 00:26:10,860
<i>‪Here is the prompt.</i>

515
00:26:11,778 --> 00:26:13,780
‪① THE SUM OF 4 NUMBERS IS 50 OR BELOW,
‪② 2 COLORS, ③ 4 SHAPES,

516
00:26:13,863 --> 00:26:14,948
‪④ THE SUM OF THE 2ND
‪AND 3RD CARD IS 25 OR ABOVE…

517
00:26:15,031 --> 00:26:18,285
‪"The sum of the 4 numbers is 50 or below."

518
00:26:19,869 --> 00:26:21,162
‪"Two colors."

519
00:26:21,246 --> 00:26:24,499
<i>‪The sixth condition was that</i>
<i>‪the </i><i>‪card </i><i>‪with </i><i>‪the </i><i>‪highest </i><i>‪number</i>

520
00:26:24,582 --> 00:26:26,584
<i>‪had to be the most common color.</i>

521
00:26:26,668 --> 00:26:28,920
<i>‪I could just tell at a glance</i>
<i>‪that it was green.</i>

522
00:26:29,838 --> 00:26:30,839
‪Green.

523
00:26:32,465 --> 00:26:33,383
‪Twenty-one…

524
00:26:35,218 --> 00:26:37,762
‪⑤ DIFFERENCE BETWEEN THE HIGHEST
‪AND LOWEST NUMBERS IS 16

525
00:26:38,596 --> 00:26:40,265
‪Oh, four shapes.

526
00:26:40,348 --> 00:26:42,434
‪If it's four shapes, it's this.

527
00:26:45,562 --> 00:26:47,105
‪Twenty-one minus sixteen is five.

528
00:26:52,152 --> 00:26:53,028
‪The shapes…

529
00:26:53,111 --> 00:26:53,987
‪③ 4 SHAPES

530
00:26:54,904 --> 00:26:55,905
‪Nineteen.

531
00:26:56,990 --> 00:26:59,409
‪Is it G? Is it G and V?

532
00:27:00,577 --> 00:27:01,411
‪G, V…

533
00:27:06,875 --> 00:27:08,626
‪Hold on. 50 or less?

534
00:27:08,710 --> 00:27:09,961
‪Damn it.

535
00:27:10,045 --> 00:27:11,921
‪This isn't it?

536
00:27:12,547 --> 00:27:13,715
‪Twenty-five or above.

537
00:27:14,382 --> 00:27:15,383
‪Twenty-five or above.

538
00:27:17,052 --> 00:27:20,180
‪Two colors. Star, circle, 25.

539
00:27:20,847 --> 00:27:21,848
‪It's not 26.

540
00:27:28,438 --> 00:27:29,814
‪It could just be 25.

541
00:27:30,565 --> 00:27:32,359
‪If it's 25…

542
00:27:32,442 --> 00:27:36,321
‪All right. Two colors, green and pink.
‪Four shapes.

543
00:27:36,404 --> 00:27:38,281
<i>‪I was so close,</i>
<i>‪with only a few letters left.</i>

544
00:27:38,365 --> 00:27:39,324
<i>‪I thought, "This is bad."</i>

545
00:27:39,407 --> 00:27:40,241
‪Eighty-five.

546
00:27:42,202 --> 00:27:43,411
<i>‪Stella Jang.</i>

547
00:27:47,415 --> 00:27:49,292
‪C, L, M, S.

548
00:27:52,504 --> 00:27:53,671
<i>‪Correct.</i>

549
00:27:53,755 --> 00:27:55,965
<i>‪You have survived.</i>

550
00:27:58,259 --> 00:28:00,512
<i>‪That concludes the exile zone match.</i>

551
00:28:00,595 --> 00:28:03,348
<i>‪Farewell, Shindong.</i>

552
00:28:03,431 --> 00:28:04,265
‪Good luck.

553
00:28:04,349 --> 00:28:05,517
‪Don't give up.

554
00:28:07,268 --> 00:28:09,229
‪It was such a pleasure.

555
00:28:09,813 --> 00:28:11,272
‪I mean it.

556
00:28:11,898 --> 00:28:13,775
‪I had so much fun.
‪I had the most fun here.

557
00:28:14,484 --> 00:28:16,528
<i>‪If I had left without contributing at all,</i>

558
00:28:16,611 --> 00:28:18,863
‪I would've been
‪so disappointed about leaving.

559
00:28:18,947 --> 00:28:22,117
‪But I think I helped out a little.

560
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:25,328
<i>‪When I first arrived,</i>
<i>‪I found the moon under the white disc.</i>

561
00:28:25,412 --> 00:28:28,748
<i>‪I also suggested we use the hourglasses</i>
<i>‪to determine when the bird would call.</i>

562
00:28:28,832 --> 00:28:32,419
‪The thought that I'm leaving something
‪for the players to come

563
00:28:32,502 --> 00:28:35,713
<i>‪makes me feel proud.</i>

564
00:28:35,797 --> 00:28:39,509
‪The one thing I truly regret
‪is not getting to see that path open.

565
00:28:39,592 --> 00:28:41,052
<i>‪I would've loved to see it.</i>

566
00:28:41,136 --> 00:28:43,304
‪I'll definitely watch it
‪when the show is released.

567
00:28:43,388 --> 00:28:44,597
‪I'm sure it'll be incredible.

568
00:28:46,474 --> 00:28:48,601
‪This is so upsetting.

569
00:28:50,520 --> 00:28:52,939
‪This is making me so sad.

570
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:55,608
‪It's really upsetting.

571
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:00,572
‪Who's that?

572
00:29:00,655 --> 00:29:01,573
‪XITSUH!

573
00:29:02,198 --> 00:29:03,283
‪XITSUH!

574
00:29:03,366 --> 00:29:04,200
‪XITSUH!

575
00:29:04,826 --> 00:29:05,744
‪XITSUH!

576
00:29:06,369 --> 00:29:07,203
‪Yes?

577
00:29:07,287 --> 00:29:09,205
‪Save me, XITSUH!

578
00:29:09,289 --> 00:29:10,707
‪Down here!

579
00:29:10,790 --> 00:29:12,333
‪COFFEE AND PROTEIN

580
00:29:12,417 --> 00:29:14,043
‪Please!

581
00:29:14,127 --> 00:29:16,629
‪Please!

582
00:29:23,011 --> 00:29:24,137
‪XITSUH is the best.

583
00:29:28,308 --> 00:29:30,018
‪He's gonna bring it in a bottle.

584
00:29:30,101 --> 00:29:33,104
‪Thank goodness. I'm dying for some coffee.

585
00:29:33,188 --> 00:29:34,773
‪XITSUH is so nice.

586
00:29:34,856 --> 00:29:39,319
‪I've barely spoken to him
‪during the games.

587
00:29:39,402 --> 00:29:41,571
‪He seems kind of intimidating.

588
00:29:41,654 --> 00:29:43,656
‪He's like a puppy.

589
00:29:43,740 --> 00:29:45,074
‪-Really?
‪-Total golden retriever energy.

590
00:29:45,158 --> 00:29:47,243
‪But a slightly unhinged golden retriever.

591
00:29:49,579 --> 00:29:54,334
‪My mood shifted dramatically
‪after the prison match yesterday.

592
00:29:54,417 --> 00:29:57,796
‪-How so?
‪-Losing two people I'd been laughing

593
00:29:57,879 --> 00:29:59,172
‪and joking around with

594
00:29:59,672 --> 00:30:03,968
‪made me wanna send
‪those guys up there home.

595
00:30:04,052 --> 00:30:06,846
‪They can't keep everyone
‪in the living area today.

596
00:30:06,930 --> 00:30:09,224
‪At least one person will end up here
‪even if they win.

597
00:30:09,307 --> 00:30:11,768
‪Starting today, we're gonna
‪gang up on them three-on-one

598
00:30:11,851 --> 00:30:14,312
‪in the prison match
‪and just execute them.

599
00:30:14,395 --> 00:30:17,398
‪The goal today is for us players in prison
‪to stick together

600
00:30:17,482 --> 00:30:21,319
‪and hit the top ranking
‪in the main match.

601
00:30:21,402 --> 00:30:22,529
‪As soon as we get in there,

602
00:30:23,154 --> 00:30:25,114
‪we stand our ground
‪and don't fall for anything.

603
00:30:25,740 --> 00:30:26,658
‪Let's do this.

604
00:30:26,741 --> 00:30:29,410
‪It's not about who goes to prison
‪and who goes to the living area.

605
00:30:29,494 --> 00:30:30,954
‪I just wanna do well in the main match.

606
00:30:31,037 --> 00:30:33,915
‪If we do, we all end up
‪in the living area together.

607
00:30:33,998 --> 00:30:36,668
‪We should share as little information
‪as possible with them.

608
00:30:36,751 --> 00:30:38,670
‪The moment we get to the game area,

609
00:30:38,753 --> 00:30:40,839
‪don't trust them or even listen to them.

610
00:30:40,922 --> 00:30:43,341
‪Don't even approach them
‪to get information either.

611
00:30:43,424 --> 00:30:45,426
‪Let's stay behind those glass doors.

612
00:30:45,510 --> 00:30:48,304
‪Starting today,
‪this is the prison alliance.

613
00:30:48,388 --> 00:30:50,431
‪Even if one of us makes it
‪to the living area,

614
00:30:50,515 --> 00:30:52,851
‪-we stick together until the end.
‪-Right.

615
00:30:52,934 --> 00:30:54,310
‪-Of course.
‪-All the way to the finals.

616
00:30:54,394 --> 00:30:57,355
‪I'm ready to give it my all.

617
00:30:57,438 --> 00:30:59,899
‪Should we make a prison pact or something?

618
00:30:59,983 --> 00:31:00,900
‪Should we bring it in?

619
00:31:00,984 --> 00:31:02,277
‪Blood pact?

620
00:31:03,027 --> 00:31:03,862
‪One, two, three.

621
00:31:03,945 --> 00:31:04,904
‪-Down.
‪-Up? Down?

622
00:31:04,988 --> 00:31:05,947
‪And the cheer?

623
00:31:06,030 --> 00:31:07,490
‪-Huh?
‪-You can decide.

624
00:31:07,574 --> 00:31:08,867
‪I'm not good at stuff like that.

625
00:31:08,950 --> 00:31:09,826
‪I'm hopeless.

626
00:31:10,577 --> 00:31:11,536
‪Wait, look.

627
00:31:11,619 --> 00:31:12,704
‪They're doing this down there.

628
00:31:12,787 --> 00:31:14,289
‪-They're doing this.
‪-A group cheer?

629
00:31:14,831 --> 00:31:16,291
‪-Let's go down.
‪-Down?

630
00:31:16,374 --> 00:31:18,001
‪-One, two, three.
‪-We got this!

631
00:31:18,626 --> 00:31:19,586
‪We should've gone up.

632
00:31:20,378 --> 00:31:21,296
‪Oh my.

633
00:31:22,338 --> 00:31:24,674
‪They really did it. What's that about?

634
00:31:24,757 --> 00:31:25,717
‪I guess

635
00:31:26,509 --> 00:31:27,427
‪they've formed an alliance.

636
00:31:27,510 --> 00:31:29,304
‪We should add sleeping pills
‪to their coffee.

637
00:31:31,347 --> 00:31:33,099
‪No weak thinking.

638
00:31:33,182 --> 00:31:37,270
‪Think of it as going into battle.

639
00:31:37,353 --> 00:31:39,564
‪-Should we bring it in too?
‪-Understood.

640
00:31:39,647 --> 00:31:42,400
‪-All right. Keep it down though.
‪-Right.

641
00:31:42,483 --> 00:31:43,610
‪Come over here.

642
00:31:43,693 --> 00:31:45,194
‪Don't forget.

643
00:31:45,278 --> 00:31:46,654
‪Kill or be killed.

644
00:31:47,947 --> 00:31:49,240
‪Keep it down.

645
00:31:49,324 --> 00:31:51,409
‪-Let's all come back here.
‪-Up or down?

646
00:31:51,492 --> 00:31:53,494
‪-Up. That's where we're going.
‪-Okay.

647
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:55,330
‪-One, two, three.
‪-We got this.

648
00:31:58,833 --> 00:32:01,377
<i>‪The main match will begin shortly.</i>

649
00:32:01,961 --> 00:32:05,340
<i>‪-Please make your way to the game area.</i>
‪-Why is it so hot in here?

650
00:32:05,423 --> 00:32:06,633
‪What will today bring?

651
00:32:07,508 --> 00:32:10,637
‪It feels like
‪today will be a turning point.

652
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:11,804
‪-Yeah.
‪-This is it.

653
00:32:16,559 --> 00:32:17,477
‪Good to see you again.

654
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:19,354
‪-Thank you.
‪-I brought corn dogs.

