<i>‪by their secret friend's score</i>

755
00:37:31,207 --> 00:37:33,417
<i>‪to yield their final score.</i>

756
00:37:33,501 --> 00:37:34,669
‪Multiplied, huh?

757
00:37:36,921 --> 00:37:37,922
‪Does minus times minus work too?

758
00:37:38,005 --> 00:37:41,217
<i>‪In other words,</i>
<i>‪every player must find their secret friend</i>

759
00:37:41,300 --> 00:37:43,344
<i>‪who will directly affect</i>
<i>‪their </i><i>‪final </i><i>‪score,</i>

760
00:37:43,427 --> 00:37:45,471
<i>‪and find ways to maximize their score.</i>

761
00:37:47,890 --> 00:37:49,141
‪This is gonna be fun.

762
00:37:49,225 --> 00:37:53,771
<i>‪Final rankings will be determined</i>
<i>‪by the highest score.</i>

763
00:37:56,065 --> 00:37:58,526
<i>‪Players in first through third place</i>
<i>‪will go to the living area,</i>

764
00:37:58,609 --> 00:38:02,071
<i>‪and players in fourth through eighth</i>
<i>‪will go to prison.</i>

765
00:38:02,154 --> 00:38:04,657
<i>‪The lowest-ranked player</i>
<i>‪will </i><i>‪be </i><i>‪eliminated.</i>

766
00:38:04,740 --> 00:38:09,870
<i>‪As a reward, players with a final score</i>
<i>‪of one or higher will receive one Piece.</i>

767
00:38:09,954 --> 00:38:13,749
<i>‪Players with ten or above</i>
<i>‪will receive two Pieces.</i>

768
00:38:13,833 --> 00:38:16,919
<i>‪The top-ranking player will be rewarded</i>
<i>‪with an advantage,</i>

769
00:38:17,003 --> 00:38:19,213
<i>‪the alliance token.</i>

770
00:38:19,297 --> 00:38:20,923
<i>‪Before the game begins,</i>

771
00:38:21,007 --> 00:38:24,427
<i>‪lottery balls will be drawn</i>
<i>‪to determine the base order.</i>

772
00:38:24,510 --> 00:38:26,846
‪Once secret friends are decided,
‪everything changes.

773
00:38:26,929 --> 00:38:28,681
‪-Everything gets flipped upside down.
‪-Exactly.

774
00:38:28,764 --> 00:38:31,475
‪The secret friend system means

775
00:38:31,559 --> 00:38:33,644
‪it's not just about
‪raising your own score.

776
00:38:33,728 --> 00:38:37,064
‪Your score gets multiplied
‪by your secret friend's score.

777
00:38:37,148 --> 00:38:41,068
<i>‪The funny thing about multiplication</i>
<i>‪is that your high positive score</i>

778
00:38:41,152 --> 00:38:44,989
‪can go down the drain
‪if your secret friend's score is negative.

779
00:38:45,072 --> 00:38:47,450
‪Once multiplied, your score
‪becomes an even bigger negative.

780
00:38:47,533 --> 00:38:51,579
‪Even working as a team,
‪we can't all make it through.

781
00:38:52,246 --> 00:38:55,291
‪I need to start looking out for myself.

782
00:38:58,336 --> 00:39:00,338
‪Hyun Kyung-lyul, you are number three.

783
00:39:00,421 --> 00:39:02,340
‪John Park, you are number two.

