00:39:02,423 --> 00:39:04,175
‪All right, let's do this!

785
00:39:06,427 --> 00:39:08,054
‪-Number one again.
‪-Jang Dong-min, you are number one.

786
00:39:08,137 --> 00:39:09,680
‪So one, two, and three are set.

787
00:39:10,348 --> 00:39:11,515
‪You're right.

788
00:39:11,599 --> 00:39:13,100
‪-That number is your ranking.
‪-Number nine.

789
00:39:13,184 --> 00:39:14,352
‪Ranking?

790
00:39:16,812 --> 00:39:18,230
‪XITSUH, you are number eight.

791
00:39:18,314 --> 00:39:21,859
‪-Seven? What? How is this possible?
‪-Yurisa, you are number seven.

792
00:39:21,942 --> 00:39:22,943
‪Number of death again.

793
00:39:23,027 --> 00:39:25,196
‪-Jung Won-young, you are number four.
‪-Oh, all right.

794
00:39:25,863 --> 00:39:27,615
‪Jeong Hyun-gyu, you are number six.

795
00:39:27,698 --> 00:39:29,450
‪-Hyun-min is number five.
‪-Yeah.

796
00:39:29,533 --> 00:39:30,951
‪I'm screwed.

797
00:39:31,660 --> 00:39:33,204
‪We're all scattered.

798
00:39:33,287 --> 00:39:36,791
<i>‪Fruit cards will now be drawn</i>
<i>‪to determine secret friends.</i>

799
00:39:36,874 --> 00:39:41,253
<i>‪The fruit cards form</i>
<i>‪the one-way secret friend chain.</i>

800
00:39:41,337 --> 00:39:43,964
<i>‪The secret friend matching chart</i>
<i>‪for the fruit cards</i>

801
00:39:44,048 --> 00:39:46,050
<i>‪is inside the envelope on the table</i>

802
00:39:46,133 --> 00:39:48,719
<i>‪and can be checked after the game ends.</i>

803
00:39:48,803 --> 00:39:50,763
<i>‪You will be informed</i>

804
00:39:50,846 --> 00:39:53,391
<i>‪of whose secret friend you are</i>
<i>‪later in the dealer room.</i>

805
00:39:53,933 --> 00:39:55,351
‪Kim Dong-jae is watermelon.

806
00:39:55,434 --> 00:39:56,769
‪Yurisa is grape.

807
00:39:56,852 --> 00:39:58,104
‪Hyun Kyung-lyul is orange.

808
00:39:58,187 --> 00:40:00,106
‪I picked kiwi, my daughter's favorite.

809
00:40:00,189 --> 00:40:02,400
‪-I have fresh lemon.
‪-Oh Hyun-min is lemon.

810
00:40:02,483 --> 00:40:03,442
‪XITSUH is cherry.

811
00:40:03,526 --> 00:40:04,819
‪-Jeong Hyun-gyu is apple.
‪-Apple.

812
00:40:04,902 --> 00:40:06,445
‪John Park is peach.

813
00:40:06,529 --> 00:40:08,948
‪Jung Won-young is banana.

814
00:40:09,031 --> 00:40:12,701
<i>‪The Piece auction to determine</i>
<i>‪the first player will begin shortly.</i>

815
00:40:12,785 --> 00:40:15,996
‪Picking the first player
‪is really important.

816
00:40:16,080 --> 00:40:18,082
‪-How many Pieces do you have?
‪-Three.

817
00:40:18,165 --> 00:40:19,917
‪Then let's block them.

818
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:21,752
‪-You're gonna bid three too? Hold on.
‪-Yeah.

819
00:40:21,836 --> 00:40:24,338
‪If you're gonna bid three,
‪let's all do that

820
00:40:24,422 --> 00:40:26,841
‪-and then talk it out after.
‪-Sure.

821
00:40:26,924 --> 00:40:28,801
‪There are only three rounds

822
00:40:28,884 --> 00:40:30,302
‪to earn points.

823
00:40:30,386 --> 00:40:32,179
‪So effectively,

824
00:40:32,263 --> 00:40:35,099
‪the third-to-last player in the order
‪decides the score.

825
00:40:35,724 --> 00:40:37,184
‪For example, if player six comes in first,

826
00:40:37,268 --> 00:40:39,895
‪then players eight, seven, and six
‪determine it.

827
00:40:39,979 --> 00:40:43,399
<i>‪The first player in the round</i>
<i>‪holds a significant advantage.</i>

828
00:40:43,899 --> 00:40:49,071
<i>‪Since the second exchange</i>
<i>‪runs in reverse order of the first,</i>

829
00:40:49,155 --> 00:40:52,658
<i>‪the first player gets to exchange </i><i>‪last</i>
<i>‪in that round.</i>

830
00:40:53,576 --> 00:40:55,494
<i>‪The outcome of each round</i>

831
00:40:55,578 --> 00:40:57,872
<i>‪can </i><i>‪be </i><i>‪heavily </i><i>‪influenced</i>
<i>‪by </i><i>‪which </i><i>‪alliance's </i><i>‪members</i>

832
00:40:57,955 --> 00:41:01,250
<i>‪are </i><i>‪concentrated</i>
<i>‪in </i><i>‪the </i><i>‪final </i><i>‪exchange </i><i>‪order.</i>

833
00:41:01,333 --> 00:41:05,087
‪The person with a teammate to their right.

834
00:41:05,171 --> 00:41:06,005
‪John.

835
00:41:06,630 --> 00:41:09,383
‪John needs to take the first player spot.

836
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:10,676
‪That's a fair point.

837
00:41:10,759 --> 00:41:12,761
‪-But John--
‪-Three Pieces are a lot for him, right?

838
00:41:12,845 --> 00:41:13,679
‪He doesn't have enough.

839
00:41:15,139 --> 00:41:16,265
‪-Something to think about.
‪-Who has three?

840
00:41:16,348 --> 00:41:17,475
‪The order didn't work in our favor.

841
00:41:17,558 --> 00:41:18,601
‪-I have three.
‪-It's just Kyung-lyul.

842
