‪if all four were playing individually.

1055
00:49:57,994 --> 00:50:00,664
‪We assumed you'd have two people bid.

1056
00:50:00,747 --> 00:50:03,542
‪Whatever we do here,
‪we always need the numbers.

1057
00:50:03,625 --> 00:50:04,918
‪That's why we had three people bid.

1058
00:50:05,001 --> 00:50:07,337
‪We came in with a strategy.

1059
00:50:07,421 --> 00:50:11,299
‪But when a strategy fails,
‪you bear the risk.

1060
00:50:11,383 --> 00:50:13,427
‪The risk is you being the first player.

1061
00:50:13,510 --> 00:50:16,096
‪No, you being the first player
‪is also a risk.

1062
00:50:16,179 --> 00:50:18,849
‪Why aren't you considering that as a risk?

1063
00:50:18,932 --> 00:50:22,352
‪You should've considered that possibility
‪when you bid your Pieces.

1064
00:50:22,436 --> 00:50:23,437
‪-If that's the case…
‪-Yes?

1065
00:50:23,520 --> 00:50:25,480
‪Then tell us. Who do you want?

1066
00:50:25,564 --> 00:50:27,482
‪Me? You.

1067
00:50:27,566 --> 00:50:29,693
‪-That's not something we can agree on.
‪-Right, we can't either.

1068
00:50:29,776 --> 00:50:33,363
‪-If you continue being so unreasonable…
‪-Then, this game will never end.

1069
00:50:33,447 --> 00:50:36,825
‪You're basically saying
‪you want everything your way.

1070
00:50:37,409 --> 00:50:41,163
‪The best outcome for you
‪is you being the first player.

1071
00:50:41,246 --> 00:50:42,956
‪Second best is me.

1072
00:50:43,039 --> 00:50:44,791
‪Who's third?

1073
00:50:44,875 --> 00:50:46,001
‪XITSUH.

1074
00:50:46,084 --> 00:50:49,045
‪-So the worst is Hyun-min?
‪-Yes.

1075
00:50:49,129 --> 00:50:50,547
‪Then let's go with XITSUH.

1076
00:50:50,630 --> 00:50:53,091
‪That's the middle ground, right?

1077
00:50:53,592 --> 00:50:54,551
‪I don't like either.

1078
00:50:54,634 --> 00:50:56,720
‪We won't get anywhere with that attitude.

1079
00:50:56,803 --> 00:50:58,430
‪What are we supposed to do with that?

1080
00:51:00,098 --> 00:51:02,601
<i>‪XITSUH being the first player</i>
<i>‪is a loss for us.</i>

1081
00:51:02,684 --> 00:51:05,228
‪Hyun-min taking it is an even bigger loss.

1082
00:51:05,312 --> 00:51:07,230
‪It was a very difficult situation.

1083
00:51:07,314 --> 00:51:09,441
<i>‪And if I'm being honest,</i>
<i>‪I almost got convinced.</i>

1084
00:51:09,524 --> 00:51:11,568
‪That's what made me angry at myself.

1085
00:51:11,651 --> 00:51:15,447
‪It made me feel like
‪I was falling for Dong-min's play again,

1086
00:51:15,572 --> 00:51:17,616
<i>‪so my anger flared up suddenly.</i>

1087
00:51:17,699 --> 00:51:19,701
‪It wasn't directed at Dong-min's play.

1088
00:51:19,785 --> 00:51:23,997
‪It was directed at me
‪for almost getting pulled in.

1089
00:51:24,080 --> 00:51:25,373
‪-Let me get this straight.
‪-Yes?

1090
00:51:26,374 --> 00:51:29,669
‪You want either you or me
‪to be the first player.

1091
00:51:29,753 --> 00:51:30,796
‪-No.
‪-Then?

1092
00:51:30,879 --> 00:51:33,423
‪That would work in my favor,
‪but that's not what I'm pushing for.

1093
00:51:33,507 --> 00:51:35,550
‪Then what are we supposed to do?

1094
00:51:35,634 --> 00:51:37,344
‪I'm saying we leave it all up to chance.

1095
00:51:37,427 --> 00:51:39,721
‪-I can't agree to that.
‪-Then I can't either.

1096
00:51:39,805 --> 00:51:41,389
‪All right, let's just forget
‪about today's game.

1097
00:51:41,473 --> 00:51:43,517
‪We won't be able to do anything
‪at this rate.

1098
00:51:43,600 --> 00:51:46,853
‪I made you the best offer I could.

1099
00:51:46,937 --> 00:51:48,772
‪It's the best concession I could make.

1100
00:51:49,940 --> 00:51:51,858
‪Just give us a second to discuss it.

1101
00:51:51,942 --> 00:51:52,984
‪Okay.

1102
00:51:53,068 --> 00:51:56,863
‪If I were Kyung-lyul,
‪I would've demanded a random draw.

1103
00:51:57,489 --> 00:52:02,702
‪I would've argued that a random draw
‪was the only fair way to settle this.

1104
00:52:02,786 --> 00:52:04,454
<i>‪The other team will find it unreasonable,</i>

1105
00:52:04,538 --> 00:52:06,790
‪but it's perfectly fair
‪from where my team stands.

1106
00:52:06,873 --> 00:52:09,459
‪As long as I don't agree to it,
‪the game can't start.

1107
00:52:09,543 --> 00:52:10,377
‪Right.

1108
00:52:11,753 --> 00:52:13,255
‪Five people can't play this game.

1109
00:52:15,549 --> 00:52:18,426
‪I'm making a deliberate play here.

1110
00:52:18,510 --> 00:52:22,931
‪It's the only way
‪to rein in his unruly spirit.

1111
00:52:23,014 --> 00:52:24,683
‪I'm being aggressive on purpose,

1112
00:52:24,766 --> 00:52:28,728
‪and I'll hold the line for our team,
‪no matter what.

1113
00:52:28,812 --> 00:52:31,648
‪-I'm not budging. Don't worry.
‪-Okay.

1114
00:52:31,731 --> 00:52:34,192
‪Those guys
‪will have more information than us.

1115
00:52:34,276 --> 00:52:36,278
‪-They have more Pieces too.
‪-Right.

1116
00:52:36,361 --> 00:52:38,989
‪We need to work through
‪the middle rankings

1117
00:52:39,072 --> 00:52:43,034
‪and boost one person through negatives
‪as much as we can.

1118
00:52:43,118 --> 00:52:44,494
‪This is what I came up with.

1119
00:52:44,578 --> 00:52:48,415
‪Kyung-lyul, Hyun-gyu, John,
‪and Hyun-min form a chain, right?

1120
00:52:48,498 --> 00:52:49,833
‪Let's work with these four.

1121
00:52:49,916 --> 00:52:52,252
‪Kyung-lyul, stay as close to zero
‪as possible.

1122
00:52:52,335 --> 00:52:53,169
‪Zero.

1123
00:52:53,253 --> 00:52:56,423
‪-John, you should have the lowest point.
‪-Okay.

1124
00:52:56,506 --> 00:52:58,633
‪-And I should be the next lowest.
‪-Okay.

1125
00:52:58,717 --> 00:53:03,471
‪It would be ideal if John got a -6
‪and I got a -4 in Round 1.

1126
00:53:03,555 --> 00:53:06,016
‪Then if Hyun-min ends up…

1127
00:53:06,099 --> 00:53:07,684
‪-With a high score?
‪-Right.

1128
00:53:07,767 --> 00:53:11,688
‪-John's big minus will drag him down.
‪-He'll end up in last place.

1129
00:53:11,771 --> 00:53:16,109
‪-And I'll turn John's score positive.
‪-Right.

1130
00:53:16,610 --> 00:53:19,779
‪Then, Kyung-lyul's near-zero score

1131
00:53:19,863 --> 00:53:23,158
‪keeps my absolute value low,
‪even if my score is negative.

1132
00:53:23,241 --> 00:53:24,534
‪That's how it'll work out.

1133
00:53:24,618 --> 00:53:27,913
‪-What do you think?
‪-But we'd need both minus cards.

1134
00:53:27,996 --> 00:53:30,749
‪It won't be easy to get both.
‪I think we should just go for one.

1135
00:53:30,832 --> 00:53:32,959
‪But we'd need both to make this work.

1136
00:53:33,043 --> 00:53:34,586
‪-Because--
‪-Yeah, we need to do it as a pair.

1137
00:53:34,669 --> 00:53:36,713
‪I do think this is better
‪than a points-scoring strategy.

1138
00:53:36,796 --> 00:53:38,715
‪It's like a suicide squad.

1139
00:53:38,798 --> 00:53:41,426
‪We need to go in there ready to go home
‪and ready to come in last.

1140
00:53:41,509 --> 00:53:44,304
‪-Nobody wants to, but that's the mindset.
‪-You have a point.

1141
00:53:44,387 --> 00:53:49,017
‪With that strategy, we'll get to
‪be the first player in the next round.

1142
00:53:49,100 --> 00:53:51,102
‪-And you can repeat that.
‪-So let's take the risk and try it.

1143
00:53:51,186 --> 00:53:53,521
‪We just need to secure
‪the -6 card in Round 1.

1144
00:53:53,605 --> 00:53:55,190
‪John, if you take the first player,

1145
00:53:55,273 --> 00:53:58,234
‪you can keep being the first player
‪from that point.

1146
00:53:58,318 --> 00:54:01,655
‪You can just continue taking the bomb
‪and sweeping all the negative points.

1147
00:54:01,738 --> 00:54:04,866
‪So is our plan to have three of us
‪keep our points low

1148
00:54:04,950 --> 00:54:06,368
‪just to push one person into last place?

1149
00:54:06,451 --> 00:54:07,827
‪Are we giving up on the living area?

1150
00:54:07,911 --> 00:54:10,038
‪-No, that's not it.
‪-It'll be worth it

1151
00:54:10,121 --> 00:54:11,414
‪if we can eliminate Hyun-min.

1152
00:54:11,498 --> 00:54:14,209
‪And with two people in the negatives,
‪someone can still come in first.

1153
00:54:14,292 --> 00:54:16,670
‪There are two options.
‪Either dodge the bombs and score points,

1154
00:54:16,753 --> 00:54:18,880
‪or take the bombs
‪and go on a suicide mission.

1155
00:54:18,964 --> 00:54:20,715
‪I also think our odds are better

1156
00:54:20,799 --> 00:54:22,717
‪-with Hyun-gyu's strategy.
‪-Take the risk, huh?

1157
00:54:22,801 --> 00:54:24,886
‪If we wanna flip things around,
‪this is the best way.

1158
00:54:25,428 --> 00:54:26,846
‪Should we go for it?

1159
00:54:26,930 --> 00:54:28,056
‪-What do you say?
‪-It does sound fun.

1160
00:54:28,139 --> 00:54:31,017
‪-It's the only strategy we can execute.
‪-This is our best option.

1161
00:54:31,101 --> 00:54:32,519
‪-The strategy works for me.
‪-Okay.

1162
00:54:32,602 --> 00:54:35,397
‪But I wanna talk about how we handle
‪the first player to make it work.

1163
00:54:35,480 --> 00:54:36,898
‪Just give them the first player spot.

1164
00:54:36,982 --> 00:54:40,986
<i>‪It seemed the other team wanted to</i>
<i>‪take control through the negotiation.</i>

1165
00:54:41,069 --> 00:54:44,322
‪I didn't think the first player spot
‪was worth fighting that hard over.

1166
00:54:44,406 --> 00:54:47,617
<i>‪I think what matters more</i>
<i>‪is </i><i>‪the </i><i>‪cards </i><i>‪you </i><i>‪end </i><i>‪up </i><i>‪with</i>

1167
00:54:47,701 --> 00:54:51,079
‪and being able to think on your feet
‪during the exchanges.

1168
00:54:52,872 --> 00:54:54,124
‪Have you talked it over?

1169
00:54:54,749 --> 00:54:56,167
‪-We'll go with XITSUH.
‪-Let's go with XITSUH.

1170
00:54:56,251 --> 00:54:57,335
‪-All right.
‪-We can accept that.

1171
00:54:57,419 --> 00:55:00,839
‪-Since we were able to compromise…
‪-Oh no, there goes my Pieces.

1172
00:55:00,922 --> 00:55:04,384
‪-I'll compete with you fair and square.
‪-Of course.

1173
00:55:04,467 --> 00:55:06,803
‪I'm sorry for raising my voice earlier.

1174
00:55:06,886 --> 00:55:08,096
‪-It's fine, it's all good.
‪-I'm sorry.

1175
00:55:08,179 --> 00:55:09,305
‪-Don't worry about it.
‪-I…

1176
00:55:09,389 --> 00:55:11,307
‪Finally starting the game
‪after an hour and a half!

1177
00:55:11,975 --> 00:55:13,685
‪-Has it been that long?
‪-Yeah.

1178
00:55:13,768 --> 00:55:15,812
<i>‪That concludes the Piece auction.</i>

1179
00:55:16,354 --> 00:55:19,691
<i>‪The first player of Round 1 is XITSUH.</i>

1180
00:55:19,774 --> 00:55:21,067
‪Nobody confirmed it with me.

1181
00:55:21,151 --> 00:55:24,946
<i>‪-XITSUH, please submit three Pieces.</i>
‪-He has to hand them over now.

1182
00:55:25,864 --> 00:55:27,365
‪Everyone gather except XITSUH.

1183
00:55:27,449 --> 00:55:28,742
‪Okay.

1184
00:55:28,825 --> 00:55:30,577
‪It's confirmed now.

1185
00:55:31,077 --> 00:55:35,040
<i>‪The game will begin in 30 minutes.</i>

1186
00:55:35,123 --> 00:55:39,044
‪The element of chance at the start
‪is the card placement.

1187
00:55:39,127 --> 00:55:41,171
‪We need to think through
‪the possible combos

1188
00:55:41,254 --> 00:55:43,465
‪and be ready to respond immediately.

1189
00:55:43,548 --> 00:55:46,551
‪Since XITSUH, Dong-jae, and Dong-min
‪are the first three to go,

1190
00:55:46,634 --> 00:55:48,011
‪we should update the buyer's slot

1191
00:55:48,094 --> 00:55:50,764
‪to eliminate blind spots
‪as much as possible.

1192
00:55:50,847 --> 00:55:55,060
‪Agreed. So XITSUH, you exchange your card
‪with one in the buyer's slot.

1193
00:55:55,143 --> 00:55:57,812
‪-Dong-jae, you do the same.
‪-Okay.

1194
00:55:57,896 --> 00:56:00,356
‪And I will too.

1195
00:56:00,440 --> 00:56:03,651
‪Hyun-min, you exchange yours
‪with the one in the discard pile.

1196
00:56:03,735 --> 00:56:07,197
‪There are 13 cards in play.

1197
00:56:07,280 --> 00:56:08,948
‪Once we know the three cards
‪in the buyer's slot

1198
00:56:09,032 --> 00:56:11,034
‪and the discard pile card,

1199
00:56:11,117 --> 00:56:13,369
‪then we'll know 9 out of the 13.

1200
00:56:13,453 --> 00:56:15,955
‪Even if the four cards change,
‪it won't be hard to guess what they are.

1201
00:56:16,039 --> 00:56:19,959
‪-So we'll know what all the cards are.
‪-We have the whole picture from the start.

1202
00:56:20,043 --> 00:56:23,254
‪-I think that strategy would be best.
‪-Yeah, given our situation.

1203
00:56:23,338 --> 00:56:25,799
‪If a bomb card

1204
00:56:26,466 --> 00:56:27,967
‪manages to land on one of us,

1205
00:56:28,051 --> 00:56:29,636
‪-we need to pass it among ourselves.
‪-Yeah.

1206
00:56:29,719 --> 00:56:32,305
‪Then we do need one person
‪to be the relay player.

1207
00:56:32,388 --> 00:56:38,394
<i>‪The current prison alliance strategy</i>
<i>‪is </i><i>‪to secure both bomb cards</i>

1208
00:56:38,478 --> 00:56:40,688
<i>‪and multiply two negatives</i>
<i>‪to earn positive points.</i>

1209
00:56:41,314 --> 00:56:42,649
<i>‪Once the cards are distributed,</i>

1210
00:56:42,732 --> 00:56:45,819
<i>‪getting each bomb to the desired player</i>
<i>‪requires moving it through players.</i>

1211
00:56:45,902 --> 00:56:49,989
<i>‪However, if someone takes Jeong Hyun-gyu</i>
<i>‪or John Park's minus card along the way,</i>

1212
00:56:50,073 --> 00:56:54,869
<i>‪they will immediately earn three points,</i>
<i>‪and </i><i>‪the minus strategy falls apart.</i>

1213
00:56:54,953 --> 00:56:59,541
<i>‪That's why they need a relay player</i>
<i>‪to pass the bomb cards.</i>

1214
00:56:59,624 --> 00:57:02,043
‪But there's a chance

1215
00:57:02,710 --> 00:57:04,587
‪those guys will start
‪by going for the bomb cards.

1216
00:57:04,671 --> 00:57:07,924
‪They'll want the -6
‪for the first player advantage.

1217
00:57:08,716 --> 00:57:12,470
‪The first player of Round 2
‪is whoever has the -6 card.

1218
00:57:12,554 --> 00:57:13,596
‪That's right.

1219
00:57:13,680 --> 00:57:19,269
‪I realized that if both minus cards
‪end up with someone on our team,

1220
00:57:19,352 --> 00:57:22,856
‪we can just keep exchanging
‪between ourselves

1221
00:57:22,939 --> 00:57:24,732
‪and earn six points each.

1222
00:57:24,816 --> 00:57:27,944
‪Our scores will remain or go up by two,
‪and we can keep the first player spot.

1223
00:57:28,027 --> 00:57:30,196
‪If we have both bombs,
‪we just keep exchanging them.

1224
00:57:30,280 --> 00:57:33,199
‪Even if they take it in the middle
‪to take some risks,

1225
00:57:33,283 --> 00:57:35,326
‪that'll only happen
‪after a few exchanges anyway.

1226
00:57:35,410 --> 00:57:37,036
‪And even then, they can't earn that much.

1227
00:57:37,120 --> 00:57:40,081
<i>‪Round 1 will now begin.</i>

1228
00:57:40,165 --> 00:57:41,749
<i>‪The cards will be distributed.</i>

1229
00:57:43,084 --> 00:57:44,294
‪Please shuffle them well.

1230
00:57:45,253 --> 00:57:46,421
‪My hand is in bad shape.

1231
00:57:52,343 --> 00:57:56,306
<i>‪Starting from XITSUH,</i>
<i>‪please check your card in order.</i>

1232
00:58:01,144 --> 00:58:02,812
‪-Kim Dong-jae.
‪-Yes.

1233
00:58:02,896 --> 00:58:04,189
‪Please check your card.

1234
00:58:04,272 --> 00:58:05,690
‪Come on.

1235
00:58:07,317 --> 00:58:09,736
‪Jang Dong-min, please check your card.

1236
00:58:09,819 --> 00:58:12,363
‪Let's see what I've got.

1237
00:58:18,203 --> 00:58:20,413
‪-John Park, please check your card.
‪-Can you hold this for me?

1238
00:58:22,916 --> 00:58:25,418
‪Next, Hyun Kyung-lyul.
‪Please check your card.

1239
00:58:25,502 --> 00:58:26,836
‪Kyung-lyul, what did you get?

1240
00:58:28,338 --> 00:58:29,172
‪Bronze.

1241
00:58:29,839 --> 00:58:32,008
‪Jung Won-young, please check your card.

1242
00:58:35,553 --> 00:58:38,139
‪Oh Hyun-min, please check your card.

1243
00:58:42,060 --> 00:58:44,187
‪Next, Jeong Hyun-gyu.
‪Please check your card.

1244
00:58:51,027 --> 00:58:53,530
‪Next, Yurisa. Please check your card.

1245
00:58:54,030 --> 00:58:55,114
‪Sweet.

1246
00:58:57,242 --> 00:58:58,576
‪B for "bomb."

1247
00:58:58,660 --> 00:59:02,622
<i>‪The card exchange</i>
<i>‪will </i><i>‪begin </i><i>‪in </i><i>‪15 </i><i>‪minutes.</i>

1248
00:59:02,705 --> 00:59:05,333
‪You guys know only three can make it
‪to the living area, right?

1249
00:59:05,416 --> 00:59:07,877
‪Yeah, same for you guys.
‪We're all in the same situation.

1250
00:59:09,128 --> 00:59:10,380
‪What did you get?

1251
00:59:11,089 --> 00:59:13,508
‪I got B6, -6.

1252
00:59:13,591 --> 00:59:15,260
‪-Oh, nice.
‪-Nice.

1253
00:59:15,343 --> 00:59:17,679
‪-What's our strategy?
‪-Can you close the door?

1254
00:59:17,762 --> 00:59:20,640
‪John, you should look for
‪the -4 bomb card.

1255
00:59:20,723 --> 00:59:23,101
‪Shouldn't both of us
‪look for that as well?

1256
00:59:23,184 --> 00:59:24,102
‪Sure, you can do that.

1257
00:59:24,185 --> 00:59:25,520
‪First things first…

1258
00:59:25,603 --> 00:59:29,857
‪John will look for the -4
‪in the first exchange.

