‪I'll exchange it with Hyun-min's card.

1899
01:27:17,941 --> 01:27:19,859
‪Exchanging with Oh Hyun-min.

1900
01:27:19,943 --> 01:27:22,111
‪-Hyun-min, you got this!
‪-Jung Won-young, you have exchanged cards

1901
01:27:22,195 --> 01:27:23,988
‪-with Oh Hyun-min.
‪-Good luck.

1902
01:27:24,072 --> 01:27:26,866
‪-Next, Hyun Kyung-lyul.
‪-Everything good?

1903
01:27:26,950 --> 01:27:27,992
‪We got the -6 card.

1904
01:27:28,076 --> 01:27:30,620
‪I'll exchange it with buyer's slot 3.

1905
01:27:30,703 --> 01:27:32,330
‪Exchanging with buyer's slot 3.

1906
01:27:32,413 --> 01:27:34,082
‪Buyer's slot 3? That's random.

1907
01:27:34,165 --> 01:27:35,375
‪Means he's not scoring.

1908
01:27:39,587 --> 01:27:41,506
‪I'll exchange it with Won-young.

1909
01:27:42,382 --> 01:27:44,801
‪-Break away. It's time.
‪-I think I have to.

1910
01:27:44,884 --> 01:27:45,760
‪Exactly.

1911
01:27:45,843 --> 01:27:46,970
‪At this rate…

1912
01:27:48,012 --> 01:27:50,181
‪I can't go down like this.

1913
01:27:52,433 --> 01:27:53,810
‪Please check your card.

1914
01:27:55,895 --> 01:27:57,021
‪-GG.
‪-GG.

1915
01:27:57,522 --> 01:27:59,274
‪-Good game.
‪-This round…

1916
01:27:59,816 --> 01:28:02,568
<i>‪That concludes the card exchange</i>
<i>‪for </i><i>‪Round </i><i>‪2.</i>

1917
01:28:02,652 --> 01:28:04,821
<i>‪All cards will now be revealed.</i>

1918
01:28:09,951 --> 01:28:11,286
‪Yurisa scored.

1919
01:28:12,161 --> 01:28:14,622
<i>‪Here are the players' current scores.</i>

1920
01:28:16,749 --> 01:28:18,835
‪-We screwed up.
‪-What happened?

1921
01:28:18,918 --> 01:28:20,837
‪Was my card taken twice?

1922
01:28:22,213 --> 01:28:24,090
<i>‪Things didn't go as planned.</i>

1923
01:28:24,173 --> 01:28:28,553
‪We thought we could keep taking
‪the minus scores consistently.

1924
01:28:28,636 --> 01:28:33,266
<i>‪I stayed at -6,</i>
<i>‪and </i><i>‪Hyun-gyu </i><i>‪went </i><i>‪from </i><i>‪-4 </i><i>‪to </i><i>‪-1.</i>

1925
01:28:33,349 --> 01:28:35,268
<i>‪He scored unexpectedly.</i>

1926
01:28:35,351 --> 01:28:36,811
‪Did we lose it twice?

1927
01:28:36,894 --> 01:28:39,147
‪Did you lose the bomb twice, John?

1928
01:28:39,647 --> 01:28:42,233
‪-I thought it was only once.
‪-I lost Yurisa's card.

1929
01:28:42,317 --> 01:28:44,652
‪-I lost the -4 and Yurisa's card.
‪-We didn't take Yurisa's into account.

1930
01:28:44,736 --> 01:28:46,446
‪-Oh, both of them.
‪-They got you with both.

1931
01:28:46,529 --> 01:28:49,073
‪They kept handing over the bombs to me.

1932
01:28:49,157 --> 01:28:50,616
‪The only way they can win is

1933
01:28:50,700 --> 01:28:53,077
‪if John and Hyun-gyu
‪take the minus scores.

1934
01:28:53,161 --> 01:28:55,830
‪They have no choice
‪but to go for the minus cards.

1935
01:28:55,913 --> 01:28:57,999
‪So all they can do
‪is check the buyer's slot,

1936
01:28:58,082 --> 01:29:02,462
‪and they'll use Pieces this round
‪to see if there are bomb cards there.

1937
01:29:02,545 --> 01:29:04,130
‪I'd like to check buyer's slot 1.

1938
01:29:04,213 --> 01:29:05,840
‪I'll check buyer's slot 2.

1939
01:29:05,923 --> 01:29:07,300
‪I'll check buyer's slot 3.

1940
01:29:07,383 --> 01:29:10,762
‪Let's say they came up empty.

1941
01:29:10,845 --> 01:29:12,805
‪John is the first player
‪this round, right?

1942
01:29:12,889 --> 01:29:14,807
‪So John goes first this round.

1943
01:29:14,891 --> 01:29:18,061
‪He'll go first in the first exchange
‪and then last in the second one.

1944
01:29:18,144 --> 01:29:21,397
‪That's when he'll find
‪the minus card and swap.

1945
01:29:21,481 --> 01:29:22,440
‪The -6 card.

1946
01:29:22,523 --> 01:29:27,612
‪When we get to Yurisa's turn,
‪she has to exchange with John.

1947
01:29:27,695 --> 01:29:29,947
‪Then, on my turn,

1948
01:29:30,031 --> 01:29:31,866
‪I can take the -6 from him.

1949
01:29:31,949 --> 01:29:32,784
‪Do you understand?

1950
01:29:32,867 --> 01:29:35,495
‪-We get three points each.
‪-Feed him three points. That's not bad.

1951
01:29:35,578 --> 01:29:37,997
‪This is the best defensive play
‪we can run this round.

1952
01:29:38,081 --> 01:29:39,874
‪Throw it to them and take it back.

1953
01:29:39,957 --> 01:29:42,293
‪I'll exchange it with Dong-jae's card.

1954
01:29:42,377 --> 01:29:44,087
‪-Exchanging with Kim Dong-jae.
‪-Yes.

1955
01:29:44,170 --> 01:29:45,588
‪Now, Yurisa can take that.

1956
01:29:45,671 --> 01:29:47,173
‪I'll exchange it with John.

1957
01:29:47,256 --> 01:29:48,633
‪Exchanging with John Park.

1958
01:29:48,716 --> 01:29:50,218
‪I'll exchange it with John.

1959
01:29:50,301 --> 01:29:52,011
‪Exchanging with John Park.

1960
01:29:52,095 --> 01:29:53,262
‪He took mine.

1961
01:29:53,846 --> 01:29:55,306
‪What's his score?

1962
01:29:55,389 --> 01:29:56,557
‪Zero.

1963
01:29:57,266 --> 01:29:59,310
‪I'll exchange it with Dong-jae.

1964
01:29:59,393 --> 01:30:01,354
‪-I'll get that.
‪-Okay.

1965
01:30:01,437 --> 01:30:03,898
‪We're set. We earned big.

1966
01:30:03,981 --> 01:30:06,067
‪-I'll exchange it with Hyun-gyu.
‪-Sure.

1967
01:30:06,150 --> 01:30:08,361
‪-We've done everything we could.
‪-Right.

1968
01:30:08,444 --> 01:30:12,156
<i>‪As Yurisa has earned points</i>
<i>‪with a diamond card,</i>

1969
01:30:12,240 --> 01:30:14,200
<i>‪she will receive one Piece.</i>

1970
01:30:14,283 --> 01:30:15,827
‪-Here is your Piece.
‪-Thank you.

1971
01:30:17,036 --> 01:30:20,748
<i>‪John Park is the first player of Round 3.</i>

1972
01:30:20,832 --> 01:30:23,209
<i>‪Round 3 will now begin.</i>

1973
01:30:23,292 --> 01:30:24,877
<i>‪The cards will be distributed.</i>

1974
01:30:25,378 --> 01:30:28,589
‪We were unlucky that round
‪because they held both bombs.

1975
01:30:28,673 --> 01:30:32,343
‪Right, but at least we got
‪the first player this time.

1976
01:30:35,429 --> 01:30:37,723
<i>‪This could be it for me.</i>

1977
01:30:37,807 --> 01:30:40,935
‪I'm thinking I might not even make it
‪to a death match.

1978
01:30:41,018 --> 01:30:43,938
‪He's my secret friend.

1979
01:30:44,021 --> 01:30:44,856
‪Are you sure?

1980
01:30:44,939 --> 01:30:46,232
‪Yeah, I am.

1981
01:30:47,567 --> 01:30:48,442
‪I don't think so.

1982
01:30:48,526 --> 01:30:50,027
‪Hyun-gyu could be your secret friend.

1983
01:30:50,111 --> 01:30:52,113
‪-If that's the case--
‪-No, he's not.

1984
01:30:52,196 --> 01:30:53,197
‪I'm telling you.

1985
01:30:53,281 --> 01:30:54,866
‪John's definitely my secret friend.

1986
01:30:54,949 --> 01:30:56,534
‪-Then Hyun-gyu--
‪-Just think about it.

1987
01:30:56,617 --> 01:30:58,161
‪-I mapped it correctly.
‪-Really?

1988
01:30:58,244 --> 01:30:59,787
‪-I'm positive.
‪-Why are you fussing?

1989
01:30:59,871 --> 01:31:02,290
‪-I'm way worse off.
‪-I'm sure I'm right about this.

1990
01:31:02,373 --> 01:31:06,460
<i>‪Starting from John Park,</i>
<i>‪please check your card in order.</i>

1991
01:31:08,045 --> 01:31:09,005
‪We need to pray.

1992
01:31:14,510 --> 01:31:16,512
‪Hyun Kyung-lyul, please check your card.

1993
01:31:16,596 --> 01:31:18,181
‪-Let's take our time.
‪-Yeah.

1994
01:31:22,101 --> 01:31:24,270
‪Jung Won-young, please check your card.

1995
01:31:24,896 --> 01:31:27,190
‪This isn't good.
‪We need to find at least one bomb.

1996
01:31:30,526 --> 01:31:31,861
‪Silver 3.

1997
01:31:31,944 --> 01:31:33,154
‪This isn't good.

1998
01:31:33,237 --> 01:31:35,823
‪Oh Hyun-min, please check your card.

1999
01:31:38,910 --> 01:31:41,120
‪Jeong Hyun-gyu, please check your card.

2000
01:31:44,332 --> 01:31:45,666
‪Bronze 1.

2001
01:31:48,044 --> 01:31:50,838
‪Yurisa, please check your card.

2002
01:31:52,965 --> 01:31:55,593
‪XITSUH, please check your card.

2003
01:31:55,676 --> 01:31:58,095
‪Kim Dong-jae, please check your card.

2004
01:32:03,267 --> 01:32:06,020
‪Jang Dong-min, please check your card.

2005
01:32:12,068 --> 01:32:13,110
‪Let's go.

2006
01:32:13,194 --> 01:32:17,031
<i>‪The card exchange</i>
<i>‪will </i><i>‪begin </i><i>‪in </i><i>‪20 </i><i>‪minutes.</i>

2007
01:32:17,114 --> 01:32:18,783
‪How did we not get a single bomb?

2008
01:32:19,659 --> 01:32:20,910
‪No luck with the draw.

2009
01:32:22,078 --> 01:32:25,164
‪We didn't get any in Round 2 either,
‪which made us use up our Pieces.

2010
01:32:25,248 --> 01:32:28,376
‪I'm not sure we can take both this time.
‪This feels pretty hopeless.

2011
01:32:28,459 --> 01:32:30,628
‪Dong-jae, you need to trust me on this.

2012
01:32:30,711 --> 01:32:32,588
‪-Okay.
‪-If I'm wrong,

2013
01:32:32,672 --> 01:32:34,507
‪I'll give up on all the titles
‪I've won so far.

2014
01:32:34,590 --> 01:32:36,634
‪-I mean that. Trust me.
‪-Okay.

2015
01:32:36,717 --> 01:32:38,052
‪Don't worry.

2016
01:32:38,135 --> 01:32:39,262
‪I have the -6 card.

2017
01:32:39,345 --> 01:32:40,930
‪-Oh, shit.
‪-I have it.

2018
01:32:41,681 --> 01:32:43,307
‪This is good.

2019
01:32:43,391 --> 01:32:45,476
‪Let's just do our best.

2020
01:32:45,559 --> 01:32:47,853
‪-You two can check the buyer's slot.
‪-If things go well…

2021
01:32:47,937 --> 01:32:50,856
‪Aren't I the one
‪in the most danger right now?

2022
01:32:50,940 --> 01:32:52,692
‪One of the two.

2023
01:32:53,192 --> 01:32:54,610
‪It could be Hyun-min.

2024
01:32:54,694 --> 01:32:56,153
‪Let's make that happen.

2025
01:32:56,779 --> 01:32:58,572
‪First, we need to find the -4 card.

2026
01:32:59,073 --> 01:33:00,116
‪Should we use a Piece?

2027
01:33:00,199 --> 01:33:01,784
‪-We have to.
‪-Use them all.

2028
01:33:01,867 --> 01:33:03,119
‪Should we make a deal with Hyun-gyu?

2029
01:33:03,869 --> 01:33:05,830
‪I can go ask him if he has it.

2030
01:33:05,913 --> 01:33:11,627
‪Ask someone who could end up in prison
‪for a favor.

2031
01:33:11,711 --> 01:33:13,587
‪Offer to save them from prison

2032
01:33:13,671 --> 01:33:15,089
‪-in exchange for help.
‪-Right.

2033
01:33:15,172 --> 01:33:16,132
‪Make that deal.

2034
01:33:16,215 --> 01:33:17,800
‪Just go up to them directly

2035
01:33:17,883 --> 01:33:20,303
‪and tell them we don't want anyone
‪from our side coming in last--

2036
01:33:20,386 --> 01:33:22,305
‪-That won't work on anyone.
‪-Wait, no.

2037
01:33:22,388 --> 01:33:23,973
‪It might work on Kyung-lyul.

2038
01:33:24,056 --> 01:33:26,726
‪It just might.

2039
01:33:26,809 --> 01:33:28,269
‪If he does agree to it…

2040
01:33:29,270 --> 01:33:32,606
‪I've never done
‪something like this before,

2041
01:33:33,107 --> 01:33:34,442
‪but I promise I won't deliver.

2042
01:33:37,194 --> 01:33:39,864
‪20 MINUTES LATER

2043
01:33:39,947 --> 01:33:40,781
‪Wait.

2044
01:33:43,326 --> 01:33:44,160
‪What?

2045
01:33:44,243 --> 01:33:45,286
‪Won-young.

2046
01:33:49,040 --> 01:33:50,333
‪Are you kidding me right now?

2047
01:35:31,350 --> 01:35:36,355
‪Subtitle translation by: Justin S. Kim
